 ## Overview
-Sobel-based Gradient Estimation computes the spatial gradient vector and magnitude for a 3D volume using a 3x3x3 kernel to estimate surface normals and edge strength for lighting and shading [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Finite Difference Stencils (Central/Forward/Backward)](3858-finite-difference-stencils-central-forward-backward.md) by applying separable smoothing weights that make it less sensitive to noise than central differences, producing higher output values for similar edges at a higher computational cost [S1, unofficial].
+Sobel-based Gradient Estimation computes the spatial gradient vector and magnitude for a 3D volume using a 3x3x3 kernel to estimate surface normals and edge strength for lighting and shading [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Finite Difference Stencils (Central/Forward/Backward)](3858-finite-difference-stencils-central-forward-backward.md) by applying a 3x3x3 kernel to estimate surface normals and edge strength for lighting and shading [S1, unofficial]. It differs from [Central Difference Stencils](9968-central-difference-stencils.md) by using a 3x3x3 kernel that provides softer gradients at a higher computational cost [S2, unofficial].
 
